[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3773871071","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115169#issuecomment-3773871071","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115169","id":3773871071,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g8LPf","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T16:39:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T16:43:30Z","body":"This has come up a few times before, in godot-jolt/godot-jolt#374 and jrouwe/JoltPhysics#1286.\n\nHowever, it seems this issue does not reproduce if you dump a Jolt snapshot (which you unfortunately have to modify engine source code to do at the moment) and run the scene inside of Jolt's own `Samples` application: [snapshot.bin.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24742305/snapshot.bin.zip)\n\nWith that in mind, I suspect this might have something to do with the fact that we no longer use Jolt's own integration of gravity, but instead do it ourselves, in order to accommodate for Godot's gravity quirks. Seeing as how jrouwe/JoltPhysics#1328 involved a bunch of gravity stuff that seems like a likely culprit.\n\nWhen snapshots are dumped we do [explicitly populate](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/78c6632eb174aabb2790975cf83e28fee065b43d/modules/jolt_physics/spaces/jolt_space_3d.cpp#L582-L583) Jolt's gravity factor, in order to make snapshots more useful, which is likely why it behaves correctly in Jolt's `Samples`.\n\nDoes that sound about right, @jrouwe?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3773871071/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3774740849","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115169#issuecomment-3774740849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115169","id":3774740849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g_flx","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T20:12:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T20:12:42Z","body":"Yes, that's definitively it. Removing the custom gravity calculation fixes the issue:\n\nhttps://github.com/jrouwe/godot/tree/115169\n\nHacking Jolt to apply the correction in https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/pull/1328 even with a gravity factor of 0:\n\nhttps://github.com/jrouwe/godot/tree/115169_v2\n\nalso fixes the issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3774740849/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3776091073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115169#issuecomment-3776091073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115169","id":3776091073,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hEpPB","user":{"login":"caphindsight","id":10833413,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODMzNDEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10833413?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight","html_url":"https://github.com/caphindsight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caphindsight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T04:32:08Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T04:32:08Z","body":"@jrouwe couldn't tell from your comment, do you think it's an easy fix, or are there other considerations? Will the fix make it into 4.6?\n\nI'm surprised because gravity sounds like the easiest force to model in physics engine (just add a constant acceleration). I'm sure there are reasons it's complicated in Godot :)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3776091073/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3778019909","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115169#issuecomment-3778019909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115169","id":3778019909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hMAJF","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T12:59:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T12:59:36Z","body":"> Will the fix make it into 4.6?\n\nI would assume neither of those are viable fixes. Even if they were, 4.6-stable is about to be released any day now, but there's always 4.6.1 of course.\n\n> I'm surprised because gravity sounds like the easiest force to model in physics engine (just add a constant acceleration). I'm sure there are reasons it's complicated in Godot :)\n\nThe problem is Godot doesn't really have a singular global gravity, like Jolt (rightfully) assumes there is, since bodies can have `Area3D` overlaps that affect their particular gravity in various ways.\n\nI'm not quite sure how you'd go about fixing this, short of Jolt getting support for a per-body gravity vector or something, but that seems like a very Godot-specific thing to add.\n\nI guess one compromise would be to rely on Jolt's own gravity integration so long as we're not overlapping with any `Area3D`, but I would say that makes things even weirder than what we have now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3778019909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3780924317","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115169#issuecomment-3780924317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115169","id":3780924317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hXFOd","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/use